===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[slouch]], [[stoop]], [[curl]], or [[lean]].
#: ''Do not '''hunch''' over your computer if you want to avoid neck problems.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[push]] or [[jostle]] with the [[elbow]]; to push or thrust suddenly.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[thrust]] out a [[hump]] or [[protuberance]]; to [[crook]], as the back.
#: {{rfquotek|Dryden}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} To have a hunch, or make an intuitive guess.
#* '''2010''', Max Gunther, ''The Luck Factor''
#*: People who are instinctive hunchers go through some such process at every decision-making point of their lives. It is likely that children often make decisions and discern truths by '''hunching'''.

